    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114-a5">

                <pb facs="0207" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg861"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in 4 in No.
                    237.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Covarrubias to Mr. Lafragua.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice and Public Instruction</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Section</hi> 1, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 27,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To the Citizen Minister of Foreign
                        Affairs, present:</hi></p>
                <p>I to-day say to the citizen judge of the district of Acapulco that which
                    follows:</p>
                <p>“The government has had notice that the Evangelical church of your city has been
                    attacked. If, as it appears, the deed is under the federal jurisdiction, you are
                    urged <pb facs="0208" n="862" xml:id="pg862"/> to proceed to institute the
                    appropriate investigation, hoping you will administer prompt and complete
                    justice.”</p>
                <p>And I transcribe it to you for your information and in reply to your
                    communication of to-day.</p>
                <p>Independence and liberty.</p>
                <closer><signed>J. DIAZ COVARRUBIAS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
